  "body": "`crates/app/tests/` has 622 flat integration test binaries and 0 directory suites. On Linux, one target set uses 66.97 GB (103.5 MB average per binary; ~100 MB with `.pdb` on Windows per `docs/decisions/3169-gate-unit-sweep.md`). A warm `camcraft-app` build takes 81 s alone and 172 s in `batch` on Linux (`-j 6`). 341 of the 622 binaries hold 5 tests or fewer.\n\nFold the 607 non-isolated, non-slow suites into ~25–35 balanced domain directory suites (`tests/<domain>/main.rs`) in bounded per-domain PRs (`mcp`, `posting`/`post`, `commands`, `operation` by family, `lathe`/`turning`, `setup`/`fixture`/`stock`, `project`/`machine`/`import`).\n- Keep all 14 `ISOLATED` app integration binaries (`xtask/src/lanes.rs`) and `app:center_cut_multiaxis` (`SLOW_BINARIES` in `xtask/src/plan.rs`) as separate binaries so wall-clock watchdogs run alone and batch timing stays stable.\n- Keep `xtask` parallel lane balance (`queue.rs`): avoid creating one oversized binary whose serial runtime dominates the queue tail.\n- Keep each submodule's `Gate map` header and `#[ignore]` markers unchanged.\n\nExpected saving: ~62.8 GB disk per worktree (-94%) and ~65 s warm build on Linux (~230 s on Windows), plus large release heavy build savings.\n\nDepends on the `xtask` directory-suite prerequisite (Part of #919).\n\nEvidence and measurements: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/919#issuecomment-7065686766\n\nDone means: `crates/app/tests/` has at most 55 binaries, `ISOLATED` and `SLOW_BINARIES` entries stay intact, `#[test]` counts (normal and ignored) match before and after, one-set `app` test disk drops below 6 GB, and `cargo xtask gate batch` passes.\n\nPart of #919\n",
